"""0501020.WR1 - fast-acting fuse, 20 A, 32 VDC, Littelfuse 501 series (1206). Bare part.

Datasheet: Littelfuse "Surface Mount Fuses, Ceramic Fuse > 501 Series", revised 08/20/15 (LCSC
C207007).

Ratings (Electrical Specifications by Item, 20 A row): 32 V maximum; interrupting rating 150 A at
32 VDC (note 1: tested at the rated voltage, time constant < 0.5 ms); nominal resistance
0.00200 Ohm (at < 10 % of the rated current); nominal melting I2t 54.760 A2s (at 1 ms); 0.05936 V
and 1.1871 W at the rated current (on 3 oz copper). Opening time (Electrical Characteristics):
at 100 % of the rating 4 hours minimum, at 350 % 5 s maximum. Continuous current: at most 80 % of
the rating (notes), times the Temperature Re-rating Curve's factor on top (0.85 at 75 C, the
datasheet's example: I = 0.80 x 0.85 x IRAT). Operating temperature -55 to 150 C.

Package (Dimensions): body 3.200 +-0.178 x 1.63 +0.10/-0.20 mm, 0.835 +-0.15 mm high, 0.520 mm
terminations; recommended pad layout two 1.000 x 1.800 mm pads 1.500 mm apart, 3.500 mm overall.
Marking code 20, mounted with the marking up (notes). The fuse has no polarity.
"""

load("@stdlib/units.zen", "Current", "Resistance", "Voltage")

P1 = io(Net)
P2 = io(Net)

# Electrical Specifications by Item, 20 A row.
current_rating = Current("20A")
voltage_rating = Voltage("32V")
interrupting_current = Current("150A")  # at 32 VDC
cold_resistance = Resistance("2mOhm")
melting_i2t = 54.76  # A2s, at 1 ms
continuous_derating = 0.80  # of the rating, before the temperature re-rating

Component(
    name="F",
    prefix="F",
    symbol=Symbol(library="0501020.kicad_sym"),
    footprint=File("Fuse_Littelfuse_501_1206.kicad_mod"),
    part=Part(mpn="0501020.WR1", manufacturer="Littelfuse"),
    pins={"1": P1, "2": P2},
    properties={
        "value": "20A 32V fast",
        "current_rating": current_rating,
        "voltage_rating": voltage_rating,
        "interrupting_current": interrupting_current,
        "cold_resistance": cold_resistance,
        "melting_i2t": melting_i2t,
        "continuous_derating": continuous_derating,
    },
    type="fuse",
)
